{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:MassTheory.CkExtractionFromAlgebraicRules","@type":"LeanModule","name":"MassTheory.CkExtractionFromAlgebraicRules","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Analysis.SpecialFunctions.Pow.Real","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic","lean:module:QOU.BraidKnot.HoefsmitV21CosSymmetrization"],"declarations":35,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.ckFromReduction_matches_ladder_H3","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.ckFromReduction_matches_ladder_H3","kind":"theorem","line":319,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/ck-extraction-from-algebraic-rules.lean#L319-L330","doc":"**Conditional corollary at H_3.** Q-YST + Hecke-quadratic + GB/jet\ninstances elaborate automatically; the `YangBaxterRule 3 q` slot\nis left explicit until the d_1↔d_2 swap fix lands (see\n`rem:post-pr665-open-rd-inventory`). Downstream consumers supply\ntheir own `[YangBaxterRule 3 q]` instance. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.ckFromReduction_matches_ladder","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.ckFromReduction_matches_ladder","kind":"theorem","line":300,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/ck-extraction-from-algebraic-rules.lean#L300-L317","doc":"**c_k extraction from algebraic rules (canonical export).**\n\nUnder all four reduction-rule class instances (Yang-Baxter,\nq-Young symmetrizers, Hecke quadratic, GB/jet reduction), the\nextraction function reproduces the per-rung `c_k` coefficients\nof the Q_β categorical precision ladder through `k = 4`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.sigma0_hecke_quad_bottomright","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.sigma0_hecke_quad_bottomright","kind":"theorem","line":287,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/ck-extraction-from-algebraic-rules.lean#L287-L292","doc":"σ_0 Hecke-quadratic identity (bottom-right diagonal entry):\n`q⁻² = (q − q⁻¹) · (-q⁻¹) + 1`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.sigma0_hecke_quad_topleft","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.sigma0_hecke_quad_topleft","kind":"theorem","line":280,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/ck-extraction-from-algebraic-rules.lean#L280-L285","doc":"σ_0 Hecke-quadratic identity (top-left diagonal entry):\n`q² = (q − q⁻¹) · q + 1`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.sigma0_det_eigval_product","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.sigma0_det_eigval_product","kind":"theorem","line":275,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/ck-extraction-from-algebraic-rules.lean#L275-L278","doc":"σ_0 determinant eigenvalue product: `q · (-q⁻¹) = -1` (for q ≠ 0). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.sigma0_trace_eigval_sum","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.sigma0_trace_eigval_sum","kind":"theorem","line":272,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/ck-extraction-from-algebraic-rules.lean#L272-L273","doc":"σ_0 trace eigenvalue sum: `q + (-q⁻¹) = q − q⁻¹`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.gbJet_k4","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.gbJet_k4","kind":"instance","line":254,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/ck-extraction-from-algebraic-rules.lean#L254-L254","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.gbJet_k3","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.gbJet_k3","kind":"instance","line":253,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/ck-extraction-from-algebraic-rules.lean#L253-L253","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.gbJet_k2","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.gbJet_k2","kind":"instance","line":252,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/ck-extraction-from-algebraic-rules.lean#L252-L252","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.gbJet_k1","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.gbJet_k1","kind":"instance","line":245,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/ck-extraction-from-algebraic-rules.lean#L245-L251","doc":"**GB/jet reduction** instances at extraction orders k = 1..4.\n\nSubstantive discharge for k=1,2: direct case-analysis on the\ntyped-B_3 word at order ε² and ε⁴ (the reductions are short).\nFor k=3,4: matches the closed-form values via the\n`ckFromReduction_eq_c{3,4}` theorems. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.heckeQuadratic_H3","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.heckeQuadratic_H3","kind":"instance","line":236,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/ck-extraction-from-algebraic-rules.lean#L236-L243","doc":"**Hecke quadratic at H_3** — instance witness.\n\nSubstantive discharge: `hoefsmit_sigma0_hecke_quadratic` and\n`hoefsmit_sigma1_hecke_quadratic` in\n`hoefsmit-V21-cos-symmetrization.lean` cover both generators\nof H_3(q) on `V_(2,1)`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.qYoungSymmetrizers_H3","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.qYoungSymmetrizers_H3","kind":"instance","line":228,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/ck-extraction-from-algebraic-rules.lean#L228-L234","doc":"**q-Young symmetrizers at H_3** — instance witness.\n\nSubstantive discharge: the three Hecke idempotents\n`e_(3), e_(2,1), e_(1³)` for H_3(q) (open R&D — see `.md`\nblock's \"Open R&D\" §). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.ckFromReduction_eq_c4","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.ckFromReduction_eq_c4","kind":"theorem","line":183,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/ck-extraction-from-algebraic-rules.lean#L183-L186","doc":"`c_4 = b² + 1/2` (mixed intra/inter-block, Kashiwara `b²` plus\nHopf-half rational offset). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.ckFromReduction_eq_c3","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.ckFromReduction_eq_c3","kind":"theorem","line":176,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/ck-extraction-from-algebraic-rules.lean#L176-L179","doc":"`c_3 = -2 = J_Hopf(q=1)` (classical-limit Hopf-link Jones value\nat the 3-fold Markov closure, via KL decategorification). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.ckFromReduction_eq_c2","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.ckFromReduction_eq_c2","kind":"theorem","line":170,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/ck-extraction-from-algebraic-rules.lean#L170-L172","doc":"`c_2 = b²` (Kashiwara `f̃_1† f̃_1` return amplitude on `V_(2,1)`). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.ckFromReduction_eq_c1","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.ckFromReduction_eq_c1","kind":"theorem","line":164,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/ck-extraction-from-algebraic-rules.lean#L164-L166","doc":"`c_1 = b` (Kashiwara `f̃_1` matrix element on `V_(2,1)`). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.ckFromReduction","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.ckFromReduction","kind":"def","line":146,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/ck-extraction-from-algebraic-rules.lean#L146-L154","doc":"The `c_k` coefficient extracted from the typed-B_3 word at order\n`ε^(2k)` via the four algebraic reduction rules. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.GBJetReduction.gb_residual_eq_zero","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.GBJetReduction.gb_residual_eq_zero","kind":"theorem","line":138,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/ck-extraction-from-algebraic-rules.lean#L138-L138","doc":"The GB/jet residual vanishes (the reduction reproduces the\ncanonical `c_k` value). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.GBJetReduction.gb_residual","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.GBJetReduction.gb_residual","kind":"def","line":135,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/ck-extraction-from-algebraic-rules.lean#L135-L135","doc":"Scalar residual of `(normal-form output) − (canonical c_k)`\nafter the GB/jet reduction at order `(q-1)^(2k)`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.GBJetReduction.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.GBJetReduction.mk","kind":"ctor","line":132,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/ck-extraction-from-algebraic-rules.lean#L132-L132","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.GBJetReduction","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.GBJetReduction","kind":"class","line":130,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/ck-extraction-from-algebraic-rules.lean#L130-L138","doc":"**Gröbner-Shirshov / jet reduction** at extraction order `k`,\nvia the explicit-residual pattern. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.HeckeQuadraticAllGenerators.hecke_quad_residual_eq_zero","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.HeckeQuadraticAllGenerators.hecke_quad_residual_eq_zero","kind":"theorem","line":117,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/ck-extraction-from-algebraic-rules.lean#L117-L117","doc":"The Hecke quadratic residual vanishes. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.HeckeQuadraticAllGenerators.hecke_quad_residual","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.HeckeQuadraticAllGenerators.hecke_quad_residual","kind":"def","line":115,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/ck-extraction-from-algebraic-rules.lean#L115-L115","doc":"Scalar residual of `σ_i² − (q-q⁻¹)σ_i − 1` for every\ngenerator `i`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.HeckeQuadraticAllGenerators.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.HeckeQuadraticAllGenerators.mk","kind":"ctor","line":112,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/ck-extraction-from-algebraic-rules.lean#L112-L112","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.HeckeQuadraticAllGenerators","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.HeckeQuadraticAllGenerators","kind":"class","line":110,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/ck-extraction-from-algebraic-rules.lean#L110-L117","doc":"**Hecke quadratic** at every generator of `H_n(q)` axiomatised\nvia the explicit-residual pattern. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.QYoungSymmetrizers.qyst_residual_eq_zero","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.QYoungSymmetrizers.qyst_residual_eq_zero","kind":"theorem","line":100,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/ck-extraction-from-algebraic-rules.lean#L100-L100","doc":"The completeness residual vanishes. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.QYoungSymmetrizers.qyst_residual","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.QYoungSymmetrizers.qyst_residual","kind":"def","line":98,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/ck-extraction-from-algebraic-rules.lean#L98-L98","doc":"Scalar residual of the Hecke-idempotent completeness relation\n`Σ_{λ ⊢ n} e_λ = 1` (per the Wedderburn block decomposition). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.QYoungSymmetrizers.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.QYoungSymmetrizers.mk","kind":"ctor","line":95,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/ck-extraction-from-algebraic-rules.lean#L95-L95","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.QYoungSymmetrizers","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.QYoungSymmetrizers","kind":"class","line":91,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/ck-extraction-from-algebraic-rules.lean#L91-L100","doc":"**q-Young symmetrizers** (Hecke idempotents) axiomatised via the\nexplicit-residual pattern: the class carries the residual of the\ncompleteness relation `Σ_λ e_λ − 1` projected to a scalar\ninvariant, and asserts it vanishes. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.YangBaxterRule.yb_residual_eq_zero","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.YangBaxterRule.yb_residual_eq_zero","kind":"theorem","line":76,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/ck-extraction-from-algebraic-rules.lean#L76-L76","doc":"The YB residual vanishes: `σ_i σ_{i+1} σ_i = σ_{i+1} σ_i σ_{i+1}`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.YangBaxterRule.yb_residual","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.YangBaxterRule.yb_residual","kind":"def","line":74,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/ck-extraction-from-algebraic-rules.lean#L74-L74","doc":"Scalar residual of the YB cubic relation (some chosen scalar\ninvariant: a matrix entry, trace, etc.). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.YangBaxterRule.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.YangBaxterRule.mk","kind":"ctor","line":71,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/ck-extraction-from-algebraic-rules.lean#L71-L71","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.YangBaxterRule","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.YangBaxterRule","kind":"class","line":66,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/ck-extraction-from-algebraic-rules.lean#L66-L76","doc":"**Yang-Baxter (braid) cubic relation** axiomatised for `B_n` at\nsubstrate `q` via the explicit-residual pattern. The class\ncarries the **scalar residual** between the two sides of the\ncubic identity (`σ_i σ_{i+1} σ_i − σ_{i+1} σ_i σ_{i+1}`) and\nasserts it vanishes. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.jonesHopfLocal","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.jonesHopfLocal","kind":"def","line":52,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/ck-extraction-from-algebraic-rules.lean#L52-L54","doc":"Local copy of the classical-limit Hopf-link Jones value\n`J_Hopf(q=1) = -2`. Mirrors `jonesHopfClassicalLimit`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.hoefsmitB_local","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.hoefsmitB_local","kind":"def","line":46,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/ck-extraction-from-algebraic-rules.lean#L46-L50","doc":"Local copy of the Hoefsmit off-diagonal coupling\n`b = √(q⁴ + q² + 1) / (q² + 1)`. Mirrors\n`q-beta-categorical-precision-ladder.lean`'s `hoefsmitB`. ","signatureChunk":0}]}